/* Plenix · Reference tokens (platform/system/tokens/reference.css): raw values only. --plx-ref-{kind}-{value}.
   Components never use these directly: they use semantic tokens (--plx-sys-*, semantic.css, themes/) or their own
   component tokens (--plx-comp-*, components.css). Spacing and control sizes are in rem (the name keeps the px value it
   equals at the default 16px root), so they follow the person's browser and font settings. */

/* GENERATED by build-tokens.js from platform/tokens/ (semantic.tokens.json, semantic.density-standard-comfortable.tokens.json, semantic.density-standard.tokens.json, semantic.density-compact.tokens.json, semantic.density-comfortable.tokens.json, semantic.interaction-touch.tokens.json, semantic.interaction-mobile.tokens.json, semantic.interaction-default.tokens.json, semantic.interaction-pointer.tokens.json). Edit the JSON, never this file. */
/* Plenix · Semantic tokens (platform/system/tokens/semantic.css): stable roles every component uses, --plx-sys-*.
   Static roles sit on :root. Roles that change with density are set on :root and on every density context
   ([data-plx-density]), and touch and mobile override them (also inside density contexts), so a region can be denser than
   its page and the environment still wins. Colors and elevation are resolved by the theme (themes/<name>.css, one per theme; the default is themes/default.css). */

/* GENERATED by build-tokens.js from platform/tokens/ (components.tokens.json, components.density-standard.tokens.json, components.density-compact.tokens.json, components.density-comfortable.tokens.json, components.interaction-touch.tokens.json, components.interaction-mobile.tokens.json). Edit the JSON, never this file. */
/* Plenix · Component tokens (platform/system/tokens/components.css): component and anatomy aliases, --plx-comp-*,
   used only inside the owning component's stylesheet. No component selectors, states or media queries here. Tokens whose
   value depends on density are declared per density context ([data-plx-density]), because a custom property is resolved
   where it is declared: a :root-only alias would ignore a denser region. */
